# This repo is built on Linux (F-Droid's buildserver, CI), so text files must
# use LF in the working tree as well as in the object store. Without this,
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows checks these files out with CRLF, and anything
# copied out of the working tree carries the CRLF with it.
#
# This bit us once already: the F-Droid recipe was copied into fdroiddata with
# CRLF endings, and `fdroid rewritemeta` (which writes LF) reported the entire
# file as changed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files genuinely need CRLF or cmd.exe misparses them.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries.
*.woff2 binary
*.jar binary
*.keystore binary
*.png binary
*.apk binary
